{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-26T20:57:20.087Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Implementation**\n- Added `src/core/lifecycle/reject-vcs.ts` with `commitRejectedWorktree`, which commits the moved change (`osq: <id> rejected`, reason + `rejected to <path>` body, `Osq-Change` trailer), removes a clean worktree via `worktreeRemove` (never forced), and keeps the branch. Failed commit/removal or leftover changes return a kept outcome with a `why` instead of throwing.\n- Updated `src/core/lifecycle/reject.ts`: `RejectResult` now has optional `worktree`, `branch`, and `stackedPath`; `rejectSpec` withdraws a stacked approval (delete directory, move nothing, write no record), and commits/removes a worktree change. Split helpers (`assertRejectable`, `finalizeRejectedWorktree`) to satisfy the 80-line function budget.\n- Updated `src/cli/reject.ts` to print the new `Worktree removed:`/`Worktree kept:`, `Branch kept:`, and `Withdrew stacked approval:` lines while leaving vcs-off output unchanged.\n- Updated `tests/worktree-lifecycle.test.ts` (only the reject case, now reading the branch with `git show`).\n- Added `tests/reject-worktree.test.ts` covering all four \"Rejection under version control\" scenarios plus CLI output variants.\n- Updated the README \"Version control\" section to describe stacking, reject's commit/removal, and the three new halt reasons.\n\n**Verification**\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/reject-worktree.test.ts` → 9/9 pass.\n- `pnpm verify` (typecheck, build, full suite, lint) passes.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/094-stacking/.run/results/5.md`."}}
